  "id": "margin-of-error",
  "term": "margin of error",
  "definition": "Margin of error is the amount by which a sample statistic differs from either end of its confidence interval when the statistic is used to estimate a population parameter. It expresses the distance from the estimate to the interval boundary, commonly for a 95% confidence interval unless another level is specified.",
